WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.000
It can be hard to make sense of the dense
history of the world of The Matrix.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.940
That's why we have the internet: to combine
the power of billions of minds and, once and

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.160
for all, figure out the confusing timeline
of the science fiction franchise.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.760
When humans created the first truly sentient
artificial intelligence, the world was pretty

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:20.770
hip to the idea, and immediately start building
robots capable of conscious, independent thought

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.380
to do all of the work we don't want to do.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.120
People live lives of luxury while their mechanized
workforce do the heavy lifting.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:31.960
During this time, one particular robot named
B1-66ER overhears that it's going to be decommissioned.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.560
Fearing for its life, the machine attacks
and kills its owner.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:40.170
Despite its claim of self defense, the court
finds B1-66ER guilty and orders his entire

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.220
product line to be recalled and scrapped.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.780
A machine rights protest devolves into a series
of riots quelled with lethal force by the

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.600
military, and soon, the robots have run out
of human allies.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.319
While Earth's governments are focused on killing
off the machines' human sympathizers, the

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.460
robots head out to try and find their own
space.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.520
The machines form a new city in Mesopotamia,
which they name 01.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.299
Through trade with their old masters, the
robots soon become the most powerful economy

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.100
on the planet.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.040
Hoping to leverage their dominance into peace,
the mechanical denizens of 01 approach the

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.950
United Nations and request that they be recognized
as a sovereign nation, with the same freedoms

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.900
and rights as their fleshy former masters.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.080
Instead, the humans bombard the machine city
with nuclear weapons, hoping to get rid of

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.740
AI life forms once and for all.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.740
Despite causing massive machine casualties,
the nuclear attack on 01 fails to destroy

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.980
the machines, which leads to the Machine War.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.160
Desperate for a win, humanity takes aim at
the machines most obvious weakness: their

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.520
reliance on solar power.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.660
Enter "Operation Dark Storm," the human race's
last act of desperation.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.400
Releasing clouds of nanites, human aircraft
block the sun from the sky.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.280
While humanity's food dies off from lack of
sunlight, the machines develop newer, more

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.320
advanced soldiers.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:53.160
By 2199, the humans invite a machine ambassador
to the U.N., and the remaining nations on

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.990
Earth sign an agreement to surrender.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.540
The ambassador announces that every human
on Earth is to surrender their body to their

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.800
new robot overlords, before exploding a nuclear
device, decimating New York.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:07.660
With humans irrevocably humbled, the machines
move on to finding a new power source.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.280
During the Machine War, they'd started experimenting
with a combination of fusion and the harvest

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.860
of bioelectricity from human prisoners of
war.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.900
They'd constructed skyscrapers designed to
house people's bodies and collect their energy.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.880
The problem was keeping defeated humans sedated
and compliant.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.060
With that goal in mind, the machines design
a program called the Architect, whose purpose

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.640
is to make a virtual world that will keep
human brains functioning and contained.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:34.780
The Architect creates the first Matrix: a
literal paradise with no suffering, no pain,

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.640
and no unhappiness.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.760
Surprisingly, the humans reject it.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.740
Why couldn't people handle living in heaven?

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.640
Agent Smith has a grim theory about that:

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:47.960
“... as a species, human beings define their
reality through misery and suffering."

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.640
In turn, the Architect makes a second Matrix
that operates as a living hell, with demons

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.960
and monsters running rampant.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.120
Somehow, humans don't like that one either.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.760
Around this time, a program is created to
understand facets of the human psyche.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.660
Known as the Oracle, the program theorizes
that the real issue is that the Architect's

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.520
earlier Matrix programs robbed humans of the
ability to make any kind of choice.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.660
With that in mind, the Oracle helps to design
a new Matrix.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.460
This one simulates human civilization at its
peak, around the 20th and 21st centuries.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.660
The denizens are allowed to carry out normal,
unremarkable lives as citizens of Earth's

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.280
glory days.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.360
Meanwhile, the Merovingian, a remnant from
an older Matrix configuration, starts operating

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.220
a safe house for exiled programs.

00:03:28.489 --> 00:03:32.640
To avoid deletion, many obsolete machines
go to him for protection, often in exchange

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.420
for their service.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:38.020
Even with all of the improvements made by
the Oracle, the Matrix still had flaws.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:42.500
Bugs were always going to pop up, and over
time, compile into bigger and bigger problems.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.700
To combat the inevitable system crash, the
machines began to introduce a single person

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.540
into each new Matrix called "The One."

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.040
Each One would be born toward the end of a
Matrix cycle, roughly a hundred years after

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.880
it had begun, when glitches were beginning
to pile up to the point of being uncontainable.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.940
The One would hold inside of themselves a
compilation of every anomaly in the Matrix's

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:05.620
programming, and be gifted with spectacular
abilities both inside and outside of the simulation.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.480
At the end of a cycle of the Matrix, the One,
who the Oracle would build up as a fated savior

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:13.830
to the simulation's escapees, would be led
through a series of events that would take

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:14.960
them to the Architect.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:18.959
That program would then reintegrate the One's
code into the machines' central processing

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:23.400
facility, the remnants of 01, resetting the
Matrix and starting a new cycle.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.340
The One would be told that Zion, the real-world
human stronghold, was about to be destroyed.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.310
He could either save a small handful of humans
from the Matrix and help them to start again,

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:35.400
or go back to the Matrix and fight a losing
battle, dooming humanity to extinction.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:39.870
This hundred-year process occurs five times,
with each One choosing to save who he could

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.660
and hope things go better the next time.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.440
The first Matrix movie begins about 600 years
after the end of the Machine War.

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:50.550
The Matrix, at the end of its sixth cycle,
is about to experience its sixth One in the

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:51.700
form of Thomas Anderson.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.930
A computer programmer, Anderson's life changes
dramatically when he's taken in by a group

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.500
of cyberterrorists led by the enigmatic Morpheus.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.240
Anderson is told that Morpheus believes he's
the One, a savior prophesied by the Oracle

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.960
who can stop the machines once and for all.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:09.540
He starts going by his internet handle, Neo,
and begins training aboard Morpheus' ship.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.720
Shortly after this, Neo and his friends are
hunted down by Agents, programs designed to

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:17.100
guard the Matrix from irregularities, led
by a program called Smith.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.280
Morpheus gets captured by the Agents, but
his distraction allows Neo and Trinity to

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:21.780
escape.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:26.720
Almost immediately, Neo and Trinity mount
a rescue operation, and manage to save Morpheus.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:31.820
Morpheus and Trinity make it out of the simulation,
but Neo is shot by Smith and killed before

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:32.900
he returns to life as the One.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:37.780
Neo, now able to control aspects of the Matrix,
seemingly destroys Agent Smith with his newfound

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:38.280
powers.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.940
Six months after the events of The Matrix,
the Resistance fighters of Zion have discovered

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.840
that an army of machines will breach their
city walls within three days.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.480
Meanwhile, Smith has come back.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.210
The chestful of Neo that he took in the last
movie seems to have changed him: no longer

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:06.050
acting as an Agent of the system, he now operates
as a self-replicating virus, assimilating

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.500
other programs and turning them into copies
of himself.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.540
The Oracle tells Neo that he needs to find
a program called the Keymaker who can take

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.540
him to the Source.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.639
She explains that he'll need to retrieve the
Keymaker from the Merovingian, who's keeping

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.680
him locked away in his hideaway for exiles.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.920
This leads to a car chase that ends with Neo
being led to what he thinks is the Source,

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.240
but turns out to be the Architect.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:28.680
At this point, the Architect explains everything
to Neo.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.860
This is not the first version of the Matrix,
he isn't the first One, and the idea of his

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:35.340
fated trip to stop the machines is a fabrication.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:39.199
He's been manipulated from the beginning by
the Oracle and the Architect to deliver the

00:06:39.199 --> 00:06:43.220
anomalous code stored inside of him back to
the Source, the same way that the five Ones

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.060
before him were.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.400
"The function of The One is now to return
to the Source, allowing temporary dissemination

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.530
of the code you carry reinserting the prime
program."

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.020
So why not just take it from him?

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.900
The problem comes down to the prior Matrix
designs: he has to have a choice.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:02.400
The Architect says that, although Neo won't
be able to save Zion from the oncoming attack,

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.770
he can return the code to the Source, begin
the necessary rebooting of the Matrix, and

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:10.540
take a handful of humans out of the program,
allowing humanity to start over.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.620
Alternately, he can return to the Matrix to
try and save Trinity, which would doom the

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:18.140
human race to die when the program is overrun
by glitches and shuts down.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.600
Neo strays from the paths the previous Ones
took.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.180
He goes after Trinity and manages to save
her.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:27.400
Exiting the simulation, he then discovers
that he has some level of control over the

00:07:27.419 --> 00:07:30.930
machines in the real world, too, stopping
half a dozen Sentinels with his mind before

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.180
falling into a coma.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:36.760
When he wakes up, Neo's consciousness has
been mysteriously transported to a halfway

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.920
point between the Matrix and the real world.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:42.560
Morpheus and Trinity negotiate his release,
and Neo rejoins his friends.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:46.840
Whie the machines begin their assault on Zion,
Neo and Trinity take a ship to 01.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:49.520
Smith, however, has managed to break into
the real world.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:54.420
He blinds Neo, inadvertently activating Neo's
ability to sense machine code, which he uses

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:58.140
to defeat the physical Smith and help Trinity
navigate the way to the Source.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:01.300
Trinity is killed when the ship crashes, but
Neo carries on.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.920
There, Neo negotiates a peace with the machines.

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.660
He'll offer up the code that they require
to keep the Matrix running and eliminate Smith

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:08.500
from the program.

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:12.540
In exchange, they'll stop their attack on
Zion and allow the surviving humans to live.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:18.120
Neo sacrifices himself again, this time absorbing
Smith into himself while jacked into the Source,

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:22.280
negating Smith and returning all of the programs
he assimilated to their original forms.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:27.260
As the sun rises on a new virtual day, the
Architect and the Oracle discuss the new status

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:27.760
quo.

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:31.220
Humans within the program will be allowed
to leave if they choose to, or to stay inside

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:31.880
the Matrix.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:35.400
All is as close to right with the world as
it can be in a simulated dystopia.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.960
“Just how long do you think this peace is
going to last?"

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.080
“As long as it can."

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:47.100
The events of the The Matrix Online take place
shortly after The Matrix Revolutions.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:52.040
Not long after the Truce, humans start surreptitiously
constructing a second Zion, breaking the rules

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.500
of the ceasefire between humanity and the
machines.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.450
This leads to further confrontations between
the two factions, escalated by Morpheus' newfound

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:02.860
fanatical desire to get Neo's remains back
from the Machine City.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.560
Morpheus is killed by an assassin within the
program.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:10.060
Newer, more deadly machines surface, and rumors
swirl that Neo may have survived his fateful

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.140
trip to the Source.

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:16.520
Then, The Matrix Online shuts down on July
31st, 2009, abruptly bringing to a close the

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:19.500
continuing story of the franchise's most familiar
characters.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:24.940
Finally, Neil Gaiman's short story, titled
"Goliath," takes place in the distant future.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:28.540
The Matrix still appears to be running, and
humans remain the machines' chief source of

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.040
power.

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:33.560
A new existential threat presents itself when
a hostile race of aliens attacks the Earth.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:37.980
The machines pick one unfortunate man, simulate
a war in which he trains as a fighter pilot,

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:42.090
and, once they feel he's prepared, send him
out on a ship into space to destroy the alien

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:42.580
threat.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:46.460
The man completes his task, but is no longer
considered necessary to the machines.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:50.240
They leave him to die in space, but allow
him to plug back into the Matrix until he

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:50.740
expires.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.620
There's only one thing we have to say to that:

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:53.940
"Woah."

